%description:

TcpSpoof.destAddress:host-ipv6 -- on IPv6 hosts, the segment goes to the node over IPv6.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Sends fabricated TCP packets. ... Compatible with both IPv4
(~Ipv4) and IPv6 (~Ipv6)." TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() sends one segment at the time t: a
header of 20 bytes without options and data, with the window 16384, no ACK, and the SYN bit
of isSYN.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Destination address".

The classes: host (the name or the address of a node: the segment goes to it, over the
network protocol of the type of the address) and empty ("", the default: the run stops at
the time t). The code: TcpSpoof::sendToIP() sets the network protocol of the segment from the
type of the address; an empty value resolves to an address without a type, whose
getAddressType() stops the run with "Address contains no value" (finding PF-12). The facet host-ipv6: the address of a node on IPv6 hosts has the type IPv6, so the network
protocol of the segment is IPv6. This test separates "host" from "empty" on IPv6 hosts.

Node under test: host1, on IPv6 hosts (precondition), with the time 3 s, after the address
configuration; host1 has TcpSpoof in place of its TCP and no application. The spoof sends one segment at 1 s
from the port 5000 to host2:1000 with the sequence number 12345 and the SYN bit, unless the
test changes one of these values. Observation: level 1, an IPv6 datagram carries the segment.

%# parameter: TcpSpoof.destAddress
%# class: host-ipv6
%# value: "host2"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.destAddress
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSpoofDestAddressHostIpv6")
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.srcPort == 5000 && ipv6.hopLimit > 0")
             .describe("the segment of the spoof, in an IPv6 datagram")
             .within(3.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSpoofDestAddressHostIpv6 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.destAddress = "host2"    # the parameter under test
*.host*.typename = "StandardHost6"
*.configurator.typename = "Ipv6FlatNetworkConfigurator"
*.host1.tcp.t = 3s
*.host1.tcp.typename = "TcpSpoof"
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.host1.tcp.srcAddress = ""
*.host1.tcp.destAddress = "host2"
*.host1.tcp.srcPort = 5000
*.host1.tcp.destPort = 1000
*.host1.tcp.seqNo = 12345
*.host1.tcp.isSYN = true
*.host1.tcp.t = 1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSpoofDestAddressHostIpv6: PASS
